⭐ THE SHIM IS A SEASONAL-SPO COMPENSATOR, NOT A GENERAL FUDGE: 
   seasonal rows carry 710.11 of its 715.52 = 99.2 %, and `co2_seasonal_SPO` alone 711.12 (99.4 %) 
   ⇒ option A is the RIGHT CLASS of replacement: the thing being replaced really is 
     a Southern-Ocean seasonal channel. 
 
⭐⭐ AND THE MECHANISM'S NET HIDES AN ENORMOUS INTERNAL SPLIT: 
   it BUYS 518.47 on `co2_seasonal_SPO` -- 73 % of what the FITTED shim buys there -- 
   with NO FITTED AMPLITUDE, which is the out-of-sample criterion; 
   and it PAYS -514.38 on the CO2 LEVEL rows (co2_level_MLO, co2_level_SPO). 
   NET -48.71. 
 
⇒ THE MECHANISM IS NOT FAILING AT THE SEASONAL CYCLE. It is SUCCEEDING there and 
  paying on the MEAN CO2 LEVEL -- which is the signature of the anthropogenic-uptake 
  change P10 measured (industrial-window NH drift 7.72 % of amplitude, quiet window 
  settled). ⭐ A LEVEL offset is the most REFITTABLE kind of error: it is controlled by 
  k_w, kz, the pump and fert_k, all currently pinned at values tuned for the 
  no-mechanism configuration. Had it failed ON the seasonal stream, no refit would help. 
 
⚠ CONDITIONAL on the canonical's other 30 parameters. This says WHERE the value sits, 
  not what a refit will do -- and it is what the refit must be judged on. 
